diff --git a/docs/design.md b/docs/design.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d264ea7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+# Design: Pre-generated chat message ids
+
+## Goal
+
+Generate the user and assistant message ids when a chat session opens so clients can identify the assistant message from the first progress event. Report the saved assistant message timestamp and whether persistence succeeded on the final `done` event, while always delivering the answer and keeping `done` the final event.
+
+## Scope
+
+Included: allocate two distinct ids through the existing `new_id` helper in `ChatService.open_turn`; expose them as read-only `ChatSession.user_message_id` and `assistant_message_id`; pass them into message construction; include assistant `message_id` in the initial `conversation` event; add ids and assistant `created_at` to `ChatTurnResult`; include `message_id`, `persisted`, and ISO `created_at` in `done`; remove the persistence-specific error event/code/message; render the required Vietnamese warning to CLI stderr only for an unsuccessful `done` event.
+
+Unchanged: conversation creation and context behavior, agent execution and answer streaming, repository storage format, API event framing, and ordinary agent error reporting.
+
+## Interfaces
+
+- `ChatService.open_turn(*, user_id: str, message: str, conversation_id: str | None) -> ChatSession` allocates two ids and gives them to the session.
+- `ChatSession.user_message_id -> str` and `ChatSession.assistant_message_id -> str` are read-only properties.
+- `build_turn_messages(*, conversation_id: str, user_message_id: str, assistant_message_id: str, run: AgentRun, answer_text: str, citations: Sequence[Citation], phases: Sequence[str], now: datetime) -> tuple[Message, Message]` uses supplied ids.
+- `ChatTurnResult` adds `user_message_id: str`, `assistant_message_id: str`, and `created_at: datetime` (the assistant message timestamp); existing `message_id` remains nullable according to persistence success.
+- Initial `conversation` progress data adds `message_id: str` for the assistant id. Final `done` adds `message_id: str | None`, `persisted: bool`, and `created_at: str` in ISO format.
+- `EventType` no longer defines `ERROR`, and `ProgressEvent.error`, `ErrorCode.PERSIST_FAILED`, and the persistence-specific message are removed. The CLI `_render` handles `done` with `persisted == false` by writing `!! Không lưu được lượt hội thoại này.` to stderr.
+
+## Approach
+
+Keep id allocation in the application layer at session opening, using `new_id` twice. Store ids privately on `ChatSession` and expose getter-only properties. The domain message factory remains responsible for message construction but receives identity as required inputs. On runner completion, persist using those ids, then build the final event from the result and stored assistant timestamp. A persistence exception sets `persisted` false and nullable `message_id` while retaining the assistant timestamp and answer. The CLI warning belongs in event rendering, keyed only on the final persistence status.
+
+## Testing
+
+Use domain tests to prove message construction honors caller-supplied ids. Application tests prove session ids are distinct/read-only, the initial and final events carry the contract, persisted timestamps match stored messages, and persistence failure still ends with one `done` while retaining the answer. CLI rendering tests verify stderr contains exactly the requested warning on failure and is empty for successful completion. Run the focused tests during each task and the full backend suite with `uv run pytest` from `backend/` at the end.
